  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nWhat was the deadline and requirement for an individual to file the annual income tax return for the taxable year 2023?\n\n### Short Answer\nThe deadline for an individual to file the annual income tax return for the taxable year 2023 is on or before April 15, 2024. This requirement is stipulated under Section 51(C)(1) of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Accounting Treatment\nFor accounting purposes, individuals must ensure that their income is accurately reported for the taxable year. This includes all sources of income, which should be documented and supported by relevant financial records. The income tax return must reflect the total taxable income for the year, and any deductions or exemptions should be properly accounted for.\n\n### Tax Treatment\nUnder Section 51 of the NIRC, individuals required to file an income tax return include every Filipino citizen residing in the Philippines, every Filipino citizen residing outside the Philippines on income from sources within the Philippines, and every alien residing in the Philippines on income derived from sources within the Philippines. The tax treatment will depend on the individual's total taxable income, which will be subject to the applicable income tax rates as specified in Section 24 of the NIRC.\n\n### Differences and Reconciliation\nThe primary difference in filing requirements may arise for individuals receiving purely compensation income from a single employer, who may not be required to file an annual income tax return if their tax has been withheld correctly. This is outlined in Section 51-A of the NIRC, which allows for substituted filing in such cases.\n\n### Practical Note\nTaxpayers should be aware of the filing deadline and ensure that their returns are filed on time to avoid penalties. It is advisable to gather all necessary documentation well in advance of the deadline to facilitate accurate reporting and compliance with tax obligations.",
